───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
TEMPLATE METHOD DESIGN PATTERN
───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

1. INTUITION

Soch ek fixed process hai:
chai banana ho → boil water → add tea → add milk → serve

Har baar same steps, but kuch steps change ho sakte:
koi adrak daale, koi elaichi

Matlab:
structure FIXED hai
kuch steps CUSTOMIZABLE hai

Yahi Template Method Pattern hai

───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
2. DEFINITION

Template Method Pattern ek Behavioral Design Pattern hai
jo ek algorithm ka skeleton define karta hai base class me
aur kuch steps subclasses pe chhod deta hai

───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
3. CORE IDEA

Base Class:
defines → full algorithm flow

Subclasses:
override → specific steps

IMPORTANT:
order of execution → base class control karta hai

───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
4. STRUCTURE

Base Class:
- template method (non-virtual / final)
- abstract methods (must override)
- optional hooks (can override)

Derived Classes:
- implement required steps

───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
5. WHEN TO USE

Use when:
✔ process ka flow same hai
✔ kuch steps vary karte hai
✔ duplication avoid karna hai
✔ control centralize karna hai

Example:
- ML pipelines
- Game engines (render loop)
- Payment processing
- File parsing systems

───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
6. UML DIAGRAM (VERY IMPORTANT FOR INTERVIEW)

                ┌──────────────────────────┐
                │     ModelTrainer         │
                │──────────────────────────│
                │ + trainPipeline()       │  ← Template Method
                │──────────────────────────│
                │ # loadData()            │
                │ # preprocessData()      │
                │ # trainModel() = 0      │ ← abstract
                │ # evaluateModel() = 0   │ ← abstract
                │ # saveModel()           │
                └──────────┬──────────────┘
                           │
        ┌──────────────────┴──────────────────┐
        │                                     │
┌──────────────────────┐        ┌──────────────────────┐
│ NeuralNetworkTrainer │        │ DecisionTreeTrainer  │
│──────────────────────│        │──────────────────────│
│ trainModel()         │        │ trainModel()         │
│ evaluateModel()      │        │ evaluateModel()      │
│ saveModel()          │        │ (default used)       │
└──────────────────────┘        └──────────────────────┘

───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
7. RELATIONSHIPS (INTERVIEW GOLD)

IS-A RELATIONSHIP:
NeuralNetworkTrainer IS-A ModelTrainer
DecisionTreeTrainer IS-A ModelTrainer

means:
Inheritance (strong relation)

HAS-A RELATIONSHIP:
Not present here explicitly

BUT conceptually:
ModelTrainer HAS-A algorithm structure

───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
8. FLOW CONTROL

IMPORTANT POINT:
subclasses algorithm control nahi kar sakte

kyunki:
template method base class me defined hai

───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
9. ADVANTAGES

✔ Code reuse
✔ Consistent workflow
✔ Control maintained in base class
✔ Open for extension, closed for modification

───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
10. DISADVANTAGES

✘ Tight coupling due to inheritance
✘ Hard to modify algorithm steps
✘ Too many subclasses if variations increase

───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
11. REAL WORLD ANALOGY

Think of:
Interview Process

Steps:
1. Resume screening
2. Coding round
3. System design
4. HR round

Company defines flow
but interviewer vary kar sakta hai questions

───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
12. INTERVIEW KEY POINTS

- Template method = skeleton of algorithm
- Defined in base class
- Uses inheritance
- Controls execution order
- Uses abstract + hook methods

───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────